<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vandals</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Vandal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Vandals were a Germanic people who migrated through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> before crossing into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in 429 CE. They established a kingdom centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> and sacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 455 CE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> profile treats their conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, one of the western empire's richest provinces, as a major blow, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garamantian-empire">Garamantian Empire</a> profile places their arrival in its account of decline.</p></div>
